--- A host resource the library holds for a program behind a type of its own: a stream, a lookup, a child, a configuration.
pub mod Handle;
pub use Handle/{let Handle};

--- What a host operation answers beside its payload.
pub mod Status;
pub use Status/{let Status};

use /std/{Bytes, List, Option, Cell, Io, Try};

--- An argument refused before any host call, by the errno `/sys/errno` names for it.
pub let invalid: Io/Error =
    Io/Error/other(/sys/errno/inval);

--- What a wait waits on: handles a host makes ready and cells the program fills, and what releases what the wait made for itself, whether the wait ends or is cancelled.
pub struct Waiting: pub Type {
    on: List(Handle),
    filled: List(Cell({})),
    release: Io({}),
}

--- A wait on cells alone, which made nothing to release.
pub let on_filled(cells: List(Cell({}))) -> Waiting =
    Waiting { on = [], filled = cells, release = Io/pure(()) };

--- Until something `w` waits on has moved: a suspension that releases what `w` made, whether it ends or is cancelled.
pub let suspend_on(w: Waiting) -> Io({}) =
    /sys/Io/suspend(w.on, w.filled, w.release, w.release);

--- Until a cell of `cells` is filled: a suspension that cancels nothing and goes on with nothing. Only the program fills a cell, so what waits on cells alone at the top of a program is a deadlock the host reports, and so is a wait on none.
pub let wait_filled(cells: List(Cell({}))) -> Io({}) =
    suspend_on(on_filled(cells));

--- What `attempt` answers, asked again each time something `wait` names has moved while it declines: the one loop every wait on the program's own state goes through. Nothing runs between an attempt that declines and the suspension but `wait`, which never suspends, so no change made between them is missed; an attempt takes nothing unless it answers.
pub let until(@A: Type, attempt: Io(Option(A)), wait: Io(Waiting)) -> Io(A) =
    let got = attempt!;
    match got
    | some(a) => Io/pure(a)
    | none() =>
        let w = wait!;
        let () = suspend_on(w)!;
        until(attempt, wait)
    end;

--- Everything `s` yields up to the end of the stream, for a caller whose stream no one else reads, so what a cancel or a failure drops is lost to no one: a stream another may read on is read through `/std/Io/Reader/rest`, which keeps what it read in its reader. Every chunk holds a byte, so every read short of the end is progress.
pub let read_to_end(@S: Type, use Io/Read(S), s: S) -> Try(Io, Io/Error, Bytes) =
    let go(acc: Bytes) -> Try(Io, Io/Error, Bytes) =
        let c = Io/read(@S, s, 4096)!;
        match c
        | bytes(b) => go(0x[..acc, ..b])
        | ended() => Try/pure(acc)
        end;
    go(0x[]);
